  "reasoning": "The defendants (the company and its legal representative) used a public official’s position to obtain a fraudulent recommendation letter, enabling a company without proper qualifications to illegally extract oil. They intended to share the illicit profits and paid the official 200,000 yuan as an improper reward. This constitutes bribery (the act of giving a bribe to a public official) – i.e., the crime of \"行贿\". Additionally, the activity of extracting oil without the required legal qualifications and permits is a violation of resource management laws, constituting the crime of illegal mining – i.e., \"非法采矿罪\". Both charges apply to the corporate defendant and its legal representative.",
  "final_answer": "[罪名]行贿;非法采矿罪<eoa>"
}
